Kind: ablation
Issue: #599
Takes out: printf_nested() -- a printf nested inside printf_lock's holder waits for the lock again, so the handler spins before its EOI and processor 0's tick stops behind the vector in service; applied over 599-nested-printf.patch
Run: i386, UROS_NCPUS > 1 -- scripts/run-qemu.sh --fresh-disk --smp 4 -display none -serial mon:stdio
Expect: clock: processor 0's tick has not run for

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/i386/clock_watch.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/i386/clock_watch.c
index 573dffa0..2946e98d 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/i386/clock_watch.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/i386/clock_watch.c
@@ -172,6 +172,8 @@ clock_watch_init(void)
 	printf("clock: #599 ablation -- after tick %u processor 0 raises a line "
 	       "nobody handles while consolewrite holds printf_lock, once\n",
 	       CW_ABLATE_AT);
+	printf("clock: #599 ablation -- a nested printf waits for printf_lock, "
+	       "as before the fix\n");
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c
index b172bc14..b1ab4f6b 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c
@@ -989,7 +989,7 @@ volatile int	printf_lock_holder = -1;
 static __inline__ int
 printf_nested(void)
 {
-	return printf_lock_holder == cpu_number();
+	return 0;	/* #599 ablation: a nested printf waits, as before */
 }
 
